    "title": {
     "en": "Sharing sweets"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Dhara has 12 laddoos to share with 4 children equally. How many will each child get?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "divide",
     "share equally",
     "group",
     "each"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Division means sharing equally or making equal groups.\nIf 12 laddoos are shared equally among 4 children, each gets 3. We write 12 ÷ 4 = 3.\nWe can also make groups: 12 laddoos in groups of 3 makes 4 groups.\nDivision is linked to multiplication: 4 × 3 = 12, so 12 ÷ 4 = 3.\nUse counters or draw dots to share one by one until none are left."
    }
